{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01832",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 5.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.6,
      "end_seconds": 9.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "yes, have a seat tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.81,
      "end_seconds": 23.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "Honestly, it's the worst headache of my life, and my family pushed me to come. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.59,
      "end_seconds": 26.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.55,
      "end_seconds": 29.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "About... well, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.7,
      "end_seconds": 35.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.83,
      "end_seconds": 39.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Ah, it feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.32,
      "end_seconds": 42.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.04,
      "end_seconds": 49.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "it happens every other day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.97,
      "end_seconds": 54.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Has there been coming on in seconds too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.21,
      "end_seconds": 57.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Yes, for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.27,
      "end_seconds": 60.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Have you had a stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.57,
      "end_seconds": 70.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "yes, about the same, about three months with stiff neck, mild, really oh, and vomiting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.52,
      "end_seconds": 81.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "And what about weakness or head injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.6,
      "end_seconds": 85.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.51,
      "end_seconds": 87.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.94,
      "end_seconds": 91.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "nope, uh, no fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.73,
      "end_seconds": 96.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.32,
      "end_seconds": 102.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.37,
      "end_seconds": 106.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.64,
      "end_seconds": 113.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, nothing on the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.3,
      "end_seconds": 117.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.77,
      "end_seconds": 134.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.21,
      "text": "Okay, so I take hydrocortisone cream, when needed. I'm supposed to take it regularly, um, but I don't always manage. I mean, before this I was on febuxostat; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.93,
      "end_seconds": 143.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.46,
      "end_seconds": 151.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "Right, my grandfather had a stroke. My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.96,
      "end_seconds": 157.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.08,
      "end_seconds": 162.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.47,
      "end_seconds": 166.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.8,
      "end_seconds": 172.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.96,
      "end_seconds": 190.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.83,
      "end_seconds": 201.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "yes, nickel i get a rash on my skin. Amoxicillin i come out in... well, a rash all over"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.12,
      "end_seconds": 207.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "so, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.21,
      "end_seconds": 218.93,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "I have eczema. I took the morning off to come in today. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.72,
      "end_seconds": 220.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.22,
      "end_seconds": 226.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I've had gout for about ten years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.97,
      "end_seconds": 233.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Yes, eczema and gout are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.96,
      "end_seconds": 251.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "let me quickly check your readings"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.21,
      "end_seconds": 261.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.11,
      "end_seconds": 291.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "okay: temperature 36.8, saturation 96 percent. And pulse is 75 beats a minute, BP is 153 over 96."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.52,
      "end_seconds": 296.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Right, shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.65,
      "end_seconds": 300.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.47,
      "end_seconds": 315.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Your neck is stiff and you are very sensitive to light."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.1,
      "end_seconds": 336.49,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Putting it all together, I'd lean towards a possible bleed around the brain. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. A migraine is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.52,
      "end_seconds": 341.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is this serious, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.87,
      "end_seconds": 354.84,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a possible bleed around the brain, but I'd like to confirm let's get a lumbar puncture, for thunderclap headache"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 356.48,
      "end_seconds": 359.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "The earliest is Tuesday, 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.02,
      "end_seconds": 365.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Let me think, uh, okay, I'll be there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.82,
      "end_seconds": 390.16,
      "duration_seconds": 23.34,
      "text": "Let's get an urgent CT scan of the head, for thunderclap headache. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. This needs an emergency scan, an ambulance is on its way. I'll also refer you to the emergency team. I'll want another look straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.86,
      "end_seconds": 394.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Yes, um, that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.98,
      "end_seconds": 402.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.32,
      "end_seconds": 410.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.26,
      "end_seconds": 418.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.21,
      "end_seconds": 422.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.54,
      "end_seconds": 424.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
}